I'd normally use `result` and `expected` for the value from the function being tested.

This all works, but has two calls to the function under test, which meant checking that the parameters were the same, and it took me longer than I expected to read this correctly.

I would probably have written something along the lines of (untested; not showing clear_error or memset; and possibly better with `TEST_int_eq()`)

```
        int expected = (strlen(values[i]) % 2) == 0;
        result = OSSL_PARAM_allocate_from_text(&param,
                                               params_from_text,
                                               "hexoctets", values[i], 0,
                                               NULL);
        if (!TEST_true(result == expected)) {
            TEST_error("unexpected OSSL_PARAM_allocate_from_text() %s for 'octets' \"%s\"",
                       (expected ? "success" : "failure"), values[i]);
            errcnt++;
        }
```
